// Files (M6 Task 10).
//
// `read_file(path)` and `write_file(path, body)` are builtins, not functions in
// this module: the names live in the one shared scope, so a wrapper would be a
// duplicate definition. They are documented here because this is the module a
// reader looks in for them.
//
// `read_file` answers the whole file as a fresh owned string, or the empty
// string when it cannot be read. `write_file` answers 1 for success and 0 for
// failure. A missing file and an empty file therefore read the same; the
// language has no `Result` in a builtin's signature yet.
//
// Ownership: neither consumes its argument; both results are owned.
